  "text": "Maren scrambled up the iron rungs into the lantern room, the Sinker’s heavy bronze boots clanging below her. Up here, caged in storm-panes and concentric walls of cut glass, the heat of the burning whale-oil lamp was stifling. \n\nOutside, the basalt spire rose higher, shedding rivers of incandescent mud. A low, sub-audible hum vibrated through the sole of Maren’s boots. Suddenly, the rain streaming down the exterior glass stopped falling. Drops beaded and lifted, drifting skyward in shimmering sheets. Inside her wool coat, Maren’s brass pocket-compass tore itself through the lining and struck the ceiling.\n\n\"Its ballast-field is inverting,\" the Sinker gurgled, hauling her flooded bulk through the hatch. Even her lead-weighted boots rose an inch off the grating before crashing back down. \"Clear the cradle!\"\n\nMaren threw her leather apron over the roaring lamp chimneypiece. She wrenched the scalding brass burner free from its bayonet mount, skin blistering through the leather, and hurled the flaming reservoir onto the iron catwalk. Oil spilled in floating, burning globules that drifted toward the dome.\n\nThe Sinker forced her thick shoulders between the towering bullseye panels of the Fresnel lens. Taking the blurring armillary sphere from Maren, she slammed it down onto the central spindle. \n\nThe brass rings locked. Instantly, the amber hologram vanished, replaced by a sound like a plucked anchor chain. A beam of dense, violet-black radiance—light that seemed to possess terrible mass—shot through the crystal prisms, shattering two storm-panes as it lanced out across the boiling bay."
